Package: eatTechReport
Type: Package
Title: Generate Technical Reports for Educational Assessments
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Karoline A.", "Sachse",
        email = "karoline.sachse@iqb.hu-berlin.de", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Kilian-Kristoph", "Schumann", role = "aut"))
Description: Validate plausible values and population definitions for VERA-3
    assessments, calculate performance summaries, and plot distributions
    with proficiency-level percentages. Assemble an editable Quarto performance
    section into a Word document using a locally supplied corporate template.
    Synthetic examples support development without access to assessment data.
License: GPL (>= 2)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    ggplot2 (>= 3.4.0),
    knitr,
    processx,
    quarto,
    rmarkdown,
    stats,
    tools,
    utils,
    xml2,
    zip
Suggests:
    pkgdown (>= 2.0.0),
    roxygen2,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
SystemRequirements: Quarto command line interface (for Word document rendering),
    Microsoft Word on Windows (for automatic pagination and field updates)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
